 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Start-up and undervoltage lockout",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The module begins to run once its input rises past the start-up voltage (8 to 9 V for the 24 V input models) and stops again when it falls to the lockout threshold (7.5 to 8.5 V). The output comes up within 30 ms typically, 50 ms at most, overshooting by no more than 5 %."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Remote on/off",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Pin 3 works against -Vin and is passive-on: unconnected, the converter runs. Holding it at 0 to 1.2 V, or shorting it to -Vin, turns the output off, and the input then draws at most 0.5 mA. The pin itself sinks or sources no more than 0.5 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Protection",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Output current is limited between 110 and 180 % of the rated maximum. A short on the output can be held indefinitely and the module recovers on its own once it is cleared. Under sustained overload it shuts down after 4 s and then restarts automatically. Overvoltage protection acts at 140 % of nominal output, typically."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input fusing and filtering",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "There is a capacitor inside on the input. A slow-blow fuse is recommended ahead of the module: 2.5 A for 24 V input models, 5 A for 12 V input and 1.5 A for 48 V input. Input surges up to 50 V (24 V input models), 25 V (12 V input) or 100 V (48 V input) are rated for 1 s at most."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Loading",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "No minimum load is needed. Capacitance on the output must stay under the model's limit, 180 µF for 24 V single-output models. Ripple figures are taken with a 1 µF capacitor across the output and a 20 MHz bandwidth limit."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Cooling is by natural convection (20 LFM). The case may reach +105 °C; thermal impedance from case to ambient is 26.39 K/W typical. Ambient approval under 62368-1 is up to +70 °C, or +65 °C for the 5.1 V output models. Power derating at high temperature depends on the model."
  }
 ],
